<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan weekly forex reserves down at $1.697 bln.</title>
<headline>Pakistan weekly forex reserves down at $1.697 bln.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's foreign exchange reserves were down at $1.697 billion on March 22 from $1.808 billion a week ago, and against $1.978 billion on March 21, 1996, the State Bank of Pakistan said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It gave no reason for the fall of the reserves, which it said included $533 million within and $486 million outside Pakistan.</p>
<p>Pakistan's weekly foreign exchange reserves holdings position:</p>
<p>    (MLN DLRS)		MARCH 22   MARCH 15   MARCH 21, 1996</p>
<p>TOTAL			    1,697	1,808	   1,978</p>
<p>Forex in Pakistan		533	  636	     809</p>
<p>Forex outside Pakistan	 486	  494	     460</p>
<p>Gold coins and bullion	 676	  676	     702</p>
<p>Special Drawing Rights	   2	    2		 7</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
